%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 27f14e03e2c810740bb0c7bc00654c37, type: 3}
  m_Name: StoryDatabase
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ProjectMuseum.Narrative.StoryDatabase
  scenes:
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 1
    HasTutorial: 0
    TutorialNumber: 0
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 1a
      IllustrationName: 01
      Dialogue: Time at university was over. [PAUSE] Although unsure about what to
        do next, a gut feeling made clear that dropping by Professor Eucalyptus's
        office would yield something useful.
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Determined
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 2
    HasTutorial: 0
    TutorialNumber: 0
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 2a
      IllustrationName: 02
      Dialogue: A job? In this economy? Archaeology degree.... Hmmmm.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
    - EntryNo: 2b
      IllustrationName: 02
      Dialogue: Hmmmm. [PAUSE] Hmmmmmmmmmmmm...
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
    - EntryNo: 2c
      IllustrationName: 02
      Dialogue: I know! [PAUSE] The old museum... Yes! I have a job for you. But
        it will require grit, dedication and a lot of digging!
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Excited
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
    - EntryNo: 2d
      IllustrationName: 02
      Dialogue: A museum?
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Confused
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
    - EntryNo: 2e
      IllustrationName: 02
      Dialogue: Yes! The old museum in my town, where I used to work during the summers!
        It is a rundown dingy place nowadays. But the town is in need of some help,
        and few are willing to take on the task.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Excited
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
    - EntryNo: 2f
      IllustrationName: 02
      Dialogue: Alright, professor, I don't have a better idea. I'll take on the
        museum.
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
    - EntryNo: 2g
      IllustrationName: 02
      Dialogue: Good, good. Ever since I laid eyes on you in my class that year,
        I knew you had something special about you. Meet me at the _______ Bus Stop.
        I'll explain the rest when you get there. Oh, and be sure to pack enough
        stuff to stay for a while.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 3
    HasTutorial: 0
    TutorialNumber: 0
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 3a
      IllustrationName: 03
      Dialogue: Alright. We're here.
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Determined
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
    - EntryNo: 3b
      IllustrationName: 03
      Dialogue: Wonderful! The bus arrived right on time. It's good to see you [PLAYERNAME].
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
    - EntryNo: 3c
      IllustrationName: 03
      Dialogue: Come! Grab your things. Let me show you your new home! It's quite
        literally right around the corner!
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Excited
      HasCutscene: 1
      HasCutsceneArt: 1
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 4
    HasTutorial: 1
    TutorialNumber: 1
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 4a
      IllustrationName: 04
      Dialogue: ......
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Shocked
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 4b
      IllustrationName: 04
      Dialogue: So, I'm not going to lie to you. [PAUSE]. But, you'll have a good
        bit of work to do here.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 4c
      IllustrationName: 04
      Dialogue: ......
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Shocked
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 4d
      IllustrationName: 04
      Dialogue: 'Before I let you unpack and all. Let me give you a basic tour of
        the place.[TRIGGERTUTORIAL]'
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 5
    HasTutorial: 1
    TutorialNumber: 2
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 5a
      IllustrationName: 05
      Dialogue: The place is quite small, but I think there is room for expansion.
        The entire strip of trees in the back there is owned by the museum! Which
        in turn is owned by the city council.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 5b
      IllustrationName: 05
      Dialogue: But, here. Let me get you started. Here's an old tomahawk my family
        has passed down for generations. It's said it was given to my great, great
        grandpa by a local Native American chief.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 5c
      IllustrationName: 05
      Dialogue: Now, let me see you put this in that old exhibit over there.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Excited
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 6
    HasTutorial: 1
    TutorialNumber: 3
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 6a
      IllustrationName: 06
      Dialogue: Good job!
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 6b
      IllustrationName: 06
      Dialogue: There's a lot of cleaning, remodelling and of course, artifact-hunting
        to be done before this museum returns to its glory days.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 6c
      IllustrationName: 06
      Dialogue: Speaking of artifacts, a possible ancient battle site has been identified
        around these parts. And I've managed to secure a permit for you and the museum
        to go excavating there.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 6d
      IllustrationName: 06
      Dialogue: That's awesome! I can finally be a real archaeologist!
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Smug
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 6e
      IllustrationName: 06
      Dialogue: Hold your horses! You still need a digging assistant, and I, for
        one, am too busy with the university. See if someone in town is willing to
        help you out. Meanwhile, I'll get some dinner.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 7
    HasTutorial: 0
    TutorialNumber: 0
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 7a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Heck yea! The museum is coming back! My name is Alex! I'd love to
        help you find cool ancient stuff! I know so many World War 2 fun facts!
      Speaker: Alex
      SpeakerEmotion: Excited
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 8
    HasTutorial: 1
    TutorialNumber: 4
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 8a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Good. You've found someone already!
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 8b
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Tomorrow you will go digging for the first time. I'll meet you first
        thing in the morning.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 9
    HasTutorial: 1
    TutorialNumber: 5
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 9a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: 'Rise and shine! '
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Excited
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 9b
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Ugh
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 9c
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Wake up! Your buddy Alex has been waiting outside the museum. I had
        to use my old key to let us in!
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Excited
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 9d
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: 'Hey [PLAYERNAME]! I can''t wait to go excavating! '
      Speaker: Alex
      SpeakerEmotion: Excited
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 10
    HasTutorial: 0
    TutorialNumber: 0
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 10a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: 'Looks like you got the hang of it! Good luck down there! '
      Speaker: Alex
      SpeakerEmotion: Excited
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 11
    HasTutorial: 0
    TutorialNumber: 0
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 11a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Hey, before it gets too late, be sure to make your way to the surface!
        It's dangerous to stay down there too late at night.
      Speaker: Alex
      SpeakerEmotion: Excited
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 12
    HasTutorial: 0
    TutorialNumber: 0
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 12a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Looks like you had a productive first expedition. A couple of new
        artifacts will go a long way in helping the museum return to its glory days.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 12b
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Actually, before you officially reopen the museum, I think you'll
        need a bit more help. I wonder if someone is willing to help run the ticket
        counter. Someone unscrupulous... and organized.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 12c
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: '*Knock* *Knock*'
      Speaker: Portrait
      SpeakerEmotion: Placeholder
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 13
    HasTutorial: 0
    TutorialNumber: 0
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 13a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Hey. I'm Emily from down the street. I've been noticing some ruckus
        about the museum.
      Speaker: Portrait
      SpeakerEmotion: Placeholder
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 13b
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Am I correct in assuming that the museum is opening again?
      Speaker: Portrait
      SpeakerEmotion: Placeholder
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 13c
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Well... whattaya know?
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 13d
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Young lady, are you, by any chance, in need of a job?
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 13e
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: You kidding? I'd happily take a gig at a museum in this economy.
      Speaker: Portrait
      SpeakerEmotion: Placeholder
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 13f
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Well [PLAYERNAME], it looks like some problems sort themselves out.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 14
    HasTutorial: 1
    TutorialNumber: 7
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 14a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Looks like we have a small team going!
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 14b
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Once you think the museum is ready. Come speak to me and we will
        officially open!
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 15
    HasTutorial: 0
    TutorialNumber: 0
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 15a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: 'Oh my... I haven''t been this excited since I was about your age! '
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 16
    HasTutorial: 0
    TutorialNumber: 0
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 16a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: 'Hey, is anyone there? '
      Speaker: Karla
      SpeakerEmotion: Curious
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 16b
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Hey! I'm [PlayerName]. I'm working at the museum now. The Professor
        and I are trying to fix it up.
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Determined
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 16c
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Wow! You wouldn't know it yet, but that could be big news for the
        town. This museum used to be a big draw around these parts. Loads of people
        from all across the state would come by. Brought a good bit of traffic for
        the local businesses.
      Speaker: Karla
      SpeakerEmotion: Earnest
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 16d
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Gosh!! Where are my manners?! My name is Karla. I run a small logging
        business from the town here.
      Speaker: Karla
      SpeakerEmotion: Earnest
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 16e
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: It's still got the rights to this big patch of trees in the back
        here. If you ever need to expand. You let me know!
      Speaker: Karla
      SpeakerEmotion: Earnest
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
  - Id: 
    SceneNo: 17
    HasTutorial: 1
    TutorialNumber: 8
    StorySceneEntries:
    - EntryNo: 17a
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: 'How are you settling in, [PlayerName]? I see the museum is coming
        along quite well. '
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 17b
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: From one former museum keeper to another, I suggest you contemplate
        theming your artifacts.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 17c
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Theming?
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Confused
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 17d
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: Theming. That's right. If you have objects that can be tagged similarly
        displayed close to one another in a designated zone, the museum' guests will
        be much more appreciative of the history of the objects in question.
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 17e
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: 'Imagine an iron sword from the medieval age sat next to an iron
        spearhead from the ancient age. The guests are more likely to apprecaite
        the evolution of iron weaponry through the ages. '
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Thoughtful
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 17f
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: I think I get it.
      Speaker: Player
      SpeakerEmotion: Confused
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
    - EntryNo: 17g
      IllustrationName: 
      Dialogue: 'Don''t worry it is quite simple. All artifacts have tags. If you
        have different artifacts with matching tags in a particular zone, you''ll
        notice these artifacts are scored higher, and do wonders for your ticket
        sales, and your overall museum rating too. '
      Speaker: Professor Eucalyptus
      SpeakerEmotion: Pleased
      HasCutscene: 0
      HasCutsceneArt: 0
